# Architecture Boundaries

- Respect the layering defined in `PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md`: Frontend → API → Domain/Services
  → Repositories → Database, with retailer adapters, collectors, normalization, matching,
  pricing, sale-event intelligence, recommendation, and notifications as distinct modules.
- Dependencies flow one direction only. Domain logic (`backend/app/domain/`,
  `backend/app/pricing/`, `backend/app/matching/`, `backend/app/sales/`,
  `backend/app/recommendation/`) must never import from `backend/app/api/` or from any specific
  retailer adapter package.
- All retailer-specific code must live inside `backend/app/retailer_adapters/<retailer_slug>/`
  and implement the common adapter interface defined in `RETAILER_ARCHITECTURE.md`. Adding a
  new retailer must never require modifying `normalization/`, `matching/`, `pricing/`,
  `sales/`, or `recommendation/`. If it seems to require that, treat it as a signal the adapter
  interface itself needs a deliberate, reviewed change — not a one-off workaround for a single
  retailer.
- Do not introduce retailer-specific conditionals (e.g. `if retailer == "..."`) inside core
  engine modules.
- Keep Product / Product Variant / Retailer Listing / Seller / Price Observation as distinct
  entities (see `PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md` §5). Never merge different variants of a product.
